\f1\fs22 \'93Whoah!\'94 Johnny hadn\'92t noticed the rainforest out there before. \'93Why would she want to look at that?\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 An Airborne should never be this close to the ground, even beyond the reach of the Layer.\
A king parrot landed outside the window in front of him. Johnny regarded it. The parrot turned around and shat down the window.\
\'93Tax.\'94\
Chip came in; he noticed Johnny sitting in Sarah\'92s chair. He hesitated while he tried to figure out which was the right seat, politically.\
Dr Quark entered and sat at the far end, unflipped his device and immediately started reading. Eloise entered last.\
\'93Sarah is on leave,\'94 Johnny announced when Eloise had made herself comfortable.\
\'93Maternity leave,\'94 Eloise corrected.\
\'93What?\'94 Chip looked blind-sided.\
\'93Trust a man to think a woman can perform all her functions right up to the time she pops and says, \'91Oh, look, the baby\'92s here.\'92\'94\
Every man in the room knew to stand down. Even Johnny was a man un the room who knew to stand down. Or perhaps he just guessed right.\
\'93Dr Quark,\'94 Eloise said as she patted the seat next to her. \'93You\'92ve reviewed everything Mr Stockwell provided?\'94\
\'93Yes,\'94 Dr Quark answered as he watched Chip sit where he was bidden.\
\'93And?\'94\
\'93My assessment hasn\'92t changed.\'94\
Chip drew a breath Eloise raised a finger. \'93We have already had that meeting,\'94 she said.\
Chip stopped breathing while Johnny failed to hide his satisfaction.\
Eloise tilted her head slightly to Chip. \'93Are you going to continue obstructing Project Kebab?\'94\
Chip held his shoulders from slumping. \'93I\'92m going to continue telling you when you\'92re doing something dangerous.\'94 His tone was somewhere between terse, matter-of-fact, and strained because head-on-chopping-block.\
\'93That wasn\'92t my question.\'94\
\'93It\'92s the answer you\'92re getting.\'94\
Johnny enjoyed a giddy little thrill that had started from his toes.\
Quark was still reading as if they were all in a library and everyone else was flouting the rules.\
Eloise rested her hands on the table. \'93You were employed because you knew things we did not.\'94\
\'93You know why I can\'92t turn over the evidence,\'94 Chip said.\
\'93We know why you say you can\'92t,\'94 Quark answered.\
Johnny\'92s smile became something he needed to do with his mouth while he avoided looking at Chip\'92s face reddening.\
\'93I warned you about five discs,\'94 Chip said.\
\'93Five discs provided a breakthrough,\'94 Eloise said.\
\'93On the way to disaster.\'94\
\'93Mr Stockwell.\'94\
The room fell quiet, and Eloise knew exactly how long to hold it before she spoke again. \'93Shall I just ask Sarah to hand it over?\'94\
\'93She doesn\'92t have it,\'94 Chip answered.\
\'93Or Hayley? Or perhaps I should just inform Fridge Force you contravened the Food Preservation Secrets Act.\'94 Eloise put a finger to her chin. \'93I understand you know exactly what the penalty is for that.\'94\
Chip planted both hands on the table. Eloise turned and stared at him, expecting an answer.\
\'93Detention in an offshore housekeeping reeducation camp,\'94 Chip answered.\
\'93For you and your whole family,\'94 Eloise picked under a finger nail.\
\'93I don\'92t have any family.\'94\
\'93Oh I don\'92t know, Mr Stockwell. You have the Chuglinghams,\'94 Eloise offered.\
\'93Leave them out of it,\'94 Chip warned.\
Johnny stifled a giggle.\
\'93Hayley Lanning. Sarah.\'94\
Johnny almost catapulted out of his chair. \'93What?\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'93I understand it\'92s all a matter of national security,\'94 Eloise said innocently.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Johnny stuttered and swallowed his objections. Dr Quark kept reading.\
\'93Corporate secrets don\'92t trump planetary safety,\'94 Chip said darkly.\
\'93You seem to have had quite a change of heart these last months,\'94 Eloise said. \'93I think perhaps you are a better person than the one you were, Chip. You have me to thank for that.\'94\
Chip nodded. \'93I have friends and colleagues to thank for that.\'94\
\'93That\'92s heartwarming, Chip. But corporate espionage remains corporate espionage. And that\'92s something I am well equipped to deal with.\'94\
Chip straightened. \'93I don\'92t doubt it.\'94\
Eloise continued. \'93There is also the question of whether your relationship with Fridge Force actually ended when you came here.\'94\
Chip stared at Eloise. \'93You want to accuse me of both betraying Fridge Force and spying for them?\'94\
Eloise shrugged with her lips. \'93Whichever works.\'94\
\'93I\'92m no spy.\'94\
\'93We both know, someone is.\'94\
\'93I have shared nothing with anyone outside this program,\'94 Chip stated.\
Two security officers appeared at the double doors.\
Chip turned away from them back to Eloise.\'93You\'92re serious.\'94\
\'93I generally am by the time security arrives.\'94\
\'93You put me in a cell, you lose the only person here who knows what this thing can do.\'94\
Dr Quark looked up.\
\'93I know what it can do,\'94 Eloise said.\
Chip stood and nodded grimly.\
\'93Take Mr Stockwell downstairs,\'94 Eloise told the officers.\
One of them glanced at Chip\'92s dimensions and then at his colleague. \'93Yes, ma\'92am.\'94\
\'93Don\'92t worry,\'94 Chip said. \'93I don\'92t hurt bugs.\'94\
Johnny laughed.\
The king parrot tapped on the glass and squawked.\
